From a2337cc3b2cdc00485a51fac2848dd67bb188e1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 05:11:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 613/638] aros: ARexx-style CHROMIUM command port on the
 process singleton

A second `C:OpenURL`/`claude login` while Chromium was running started
a second chrome, which CHECK-failed on its 1 GiB PA executable
reservation (error=12) on the 8 GB hosted guest - openurl.library had
no port to talk to, so it fell through to launching ubn_Path.

ProcessSingleton::StartWatching() now runs a small native thread that
AddPort()s "CHROMIUM" (CHROMIUM.1..15 when taken, the openurl
findRexxPort suffix rule) and services RexxMsg commands the way OWB
does: OPENURL "<url>" / OPEN, NEWWINDOW "<url>" (adds --new-window),
SHOW / TOFRONT / SCREENTOFRONT / ACTIVATE.  URL commands are turned
into a CommandLine and handed to the existing notification callback
on the UI thread (the same path a second instance's command line
takes), so the URL lands as a tab in the running browser; the reply
carries ARexx rc 0/5/10/20 and every dequeued message is replied even
if its task never runs.  Exec's Wait()/Signal() macros clash with
WaitableEvent, hence the ExecWait/ExecSignal wrappers.

Cleanup() joins the thread; the atexit path only signals it (no join
under exit).  Verified on hosted clean ADT with the browser registered
via `OpenURLSetBrowser Chromium <path> PORT CHROMIUM`: a second
C:OpenURL and Claude Code's execFile($BROWSER, [OAuth URL]) each land
as a tab (chromium-aros-build/out/openurl-reuse-050658/reuse-95.png).


